  "_commit": {
    "id": "93e4bcec0dc2f5e4216ef9071e61c36b3f120b32",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "Cast a plain WKT-text geometry column before spatial-join SQL\n\nlayerSpatialMatch()/.spatialMatch_sql(), layerSpatialOverlaps()'s\ngeometry-column path, st_join_table(), and st_join.DuckDBTable() all\nassumed an existing geometry column was already DuckDB-native GEOMETRY,\nwith no check or cast. .as_duckdb_table() already detects and casts a\nWKT-text geometry column, but only when uploading a fresh in-memory\nobject for the first time; it's a no-op for anything that's already a\nDuckDBTable/DuckDBDataFrame, which is exactly the case these four\nfunctions hit. A DuckDBDataFrame/DuckDBTable built with a plain WKT-text\ngeometry column (e.g. from a CSV, or any non-GeoParquet source) failed\nwith a raw DuckDB binder error (\"No function matches the given name and\nargument types 'ST_Intersects(GEOMETRY, VARCHAR)'\") instead of working.\n\nAll four now probe the column's actual type first via two small shared\nhelpers (.geom_col_is_native()/.geom_col_sql_ref() in\nDuckDBTable-spatial.R, plus a DuckDBColumn-flavored wrapper,\n.geom_column_as_geometry(), in DuckDBDataFrame-spatial.R) and wrap it in\nST_GeomFromText() only when it isn't already GEOMETRY-typed, so an\nalready-native column incurs no double-cast. The probe is a cheap\n'SELECT typeof(...) ... LIMIT 1' schema query, with a DESCRIBE fallback\nfor an empty subquery (LIMIT 1 has nothing to evaluate typeof() against\notherwise); it also recognizes a CRS-tagged GEOMETRY('OGC:CRS84') column\n(e.g. round-tripped through GeoParquet) as native, not just bare\n\"GEOMETRY\".\n\nAdded regression tests covering all four call sites against a\nWKT-text-backed DuckDBDataFrame/DuckDBTable, verified against sf ground\ntruth, plus a white-box test of the two new helpers (native detection,\nno double-cast, CRS-tagged type recognition, empty-subquery fallback).\n",
    "time": 1793913048
  },
